From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:08:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1062/1062] SableOS: Sable Media drives FM through a bridge
 service; no FM Radio launcher entry

SableFmBridgeService is an exported Messenger service that forwards power,
tune, seek, scan, speaker and mute commands from Sable Media (system image
only, checked per message) to FmService in this process and sends back the
tuner state, RDS text and the station list. While it is connected the
playing notification opens Sable Media's FM screen. FmMainActivity loses
its LAUNCHER category (it stays exported as a fallback), so the separate
FM Radio app is gone from the app list.
---
 AndroidManifest.xml                           |  14 +-
 src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java        |  23 +-
 .../android/fmradio/SableFmBridgeService.java | 315 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 348 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/fmradio/SableFmBridgeService.java

diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
index b5176fd..13eb04a 100644
--- a/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -57,9 +57,10 @@
             android:theme="@style/AppTheme"
             android:exported="true"
             android:usesCleartextTraffic="false" >
+            <!-- SableOS: no launcher entry; FM Radio lives in Sable Media (SableFmBridgeService).
+                 The activity stays exported so Sable Media can still open it as a fallback. -->
             <intent-filter>
                 <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
-                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
             </intent-filter>
         </activity>
         <activity
@@ -80,6 +81,17 @@
             </intent-filter>
         </service>
 
+        <!-- SableOS: Sable Media's remote control for the tuner. Exported without a
+             permission on purpose: every message's sending uid is checked against
+             Sable Media on the system image (SableFmProtocol.callerAllowed). -->
+        <service
+            android:name=".SableFmBridgeService"
+            android:exported="true" >
+            <intent-filter>
+                <action android:name="org.sableos.fm.action.CONTROL" />
+            </intent-filter>
+        </service>
+
         <provider
             android:name=".FmProvider"
             android:authorities="com.android.fmradio"
diff --git a/src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java b/src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java
